# Nginx-Only `/static/` URL Prefix

**Activation:** `alwaysApply: false` — when triggers in `agent-discipline-core.mdc` match, **Read this file before editing**. Triggered rules are mandatory, not optional.

## Production contract

- **Browsers load `/static/*` only through nginx**, not through Gunicorn/Django WSGI.
- **Custom proxy binary:** [`services-conf/proxy.Dockerfile`](services-conf/proxy.Dockerfile) source-builds **nginx** (pinned SHA, currently **1.31.5**) against **jemalloc**, **zlib-ng (`--zlib-compat`)**, **OpenSSL**, **ngx_brotli**, and **GetPageSpeed zstd-nginx-module** with static **`/opt/zstd/lib/libzstd.a`**. Bake on the **prod CPU** (`ENV OPT_CFLAGS_LIBS="-O3 -march=native -mtune=native -flto -g0"` on jemalloc, brotli cmake, zstd `MOREFLAGS`, nginx `--with-cc-opt`, and **`--with-openssl-opt`**). **Do not** apk-install `nginx` / `nginx-mod-http-brotli` / `zstd` / `libzstd`. Runtime **`LD_PRELOAD`** jemalloc. Modules are **`--add-module`** compiled in — **do not** `load_module`. **Do not** enable nginx Control API / `api;` / `client_body_early_read`.
- **Main vs vhost:** process/http tunables live in [`services-conf/nginx-main.conf`](services-conf/nginx-main.conf) (`worker_processes auto`, `worker_cpu_affinity auto`, `sendfile` / `tcp_nopush` / `tcp_nodelay`, `open_file_cache`, `ssl_session_tickets off`, shared gzip/brotli/zstd **types/buffers/`min_length 256`** with default **`gzip/brotli/zstd off`**). **Never** hardcode `worker_processes <N>`. Server blocks stay in [`services-conf/nginx.conf`](services-conf/nginx.conf) (`http2 on`, TLS paths). Compression **policy is per-location**: [`nginx-compress-proxy.inc`](services-conf/nginx-compress-proxy.inc) (zstd-3 + brotli-4 + gzip for Gunicorn and SPA HTML) vs [`nginx-compress-static.inc`](services-conf/nginx-compress-static.inc) (`brotli_static` / `gzip_static` for `/static/`). SPA HTML must **not** use sidecar `*.html.br` (heal rewrites `index.html`).
- Canonical wiring:
  - [`services-conf/nginx-static-files.conf`](services-conf/nginx-static-files.conf) — `location /static/` → `alias /srv/static/;` (**30d**); `location /static/frontend/_next/` (**1y immutable**, prefix **without** `^~` so the suffix denylist still 404s direct `.br`/`.gz`/`.zst` URLs); SPA shells under **`/machine/`** and **`/pub/`** set **`open_file_cache off;`** so SPA heal/`os.replace` of `index.html` is not served from a stale fd; **`/favicon.ico`** returns **404** at the edge; an explicit prefix allowlist proxies to Gunicorn for **`hpcperfstats_site.urls`** (anything else hits **`location / { return 404; }`**). SPA CSP is **document-embedded** (`<meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy">` written at export/heal); nginx SPA locations must **not** send a competing hash CSP header. **Never** store nginx config under **`/srv/static`**. **`/static/`** **404**s denylisted suffixes including **`*.inc`** and **direct sidecar** **`*.br` / `*.gz` / `*.zst`** (see **`frontend-static-prod-serve-only.mdc`**).
  - [`services-conf/nginx-django-proxy-common.inc`](services-conf/nginx-django-proxy-common.inc) — shared `proxy_*` headers/timeouts included by each Gunicorn `location`; **`proxy_set_header Accept-Encoding ""`** so nginx is the only HTTP content-coding hop; includes **`nginx-compress-proxy.inc`**.
  - [`docker-compose.yaml`](docker-compose.yaml) — shared volume `staticfiles_data` mounted at `STATIC_ROOT` on `web` (`/home/hpcperfstats/staticfiles`) and read-only on `proxy` as `/srv/static`; mounts **`nginx-main.conf` → `/etc/nginx/nginx.conf`**, vhost **`nginx.conf` → `http.d/default.conf`**, and snippets (`nginx-static-files.conf`, `nginx-django-proxy-common.inc`, `nginx-compress-proxy.inc`, `nginx-compress-static.inc`, `nginx-edge-security-headers.inc`, `nginx-csp-no-active.inc`, `nginx-csp-django-html.inc`). Those snippets are **compose mounts only** — **`proxy.Dockerfile`** must not also **`COPY`** them (main conf may be **`COPY`**d for `docker run` parity).
- **Do not** add Django URL patterns (`django.conf.urls.static.static` for `STATIC_URL`), **WhiteNoise**, or other middleware/views to answer **`STATIC_URL`** (`/static/`). That would duplicate nginx and violate the deployment contract.

## Django’s role (files on disk, not the `/static/` HTTP path)

- **`collectstatic`** (see [`services-conf/django_startup.sh`](services-conf/django_startup.sh)) populates **`STATIC_ROOT`** so the volume nginx reads stays complete (admin assets, app static, built SPA hashed files).
- Built frontend output lives under `hpcperfstats/site/hpcperfstats_site/static/frontend/` before collection.
- **SPA shell auto-heal:** after `collectstatic`, startup calls [`spa_static_root_heal`](hpcperfstats/site/lib/spa_static_root_heal.py). If **`STATIC_ROOT/frontend/{machine,pub}/index.html`** are missing but package static still has them (typical Vite-era volume after a Next export upgrade), it **replaces** `STATIC_ROOT/frontend` from package static and then verifies. If shells exist but **sha256 of package vs volume `machine/index.html` differs** (typical after a from-scratch **`hpcperfstats-full`** image rebuild while **`staticfiles_data`** still holds an older Next tree), it **replaces** the volume the same way — that is how a full Docker rebuild lands SPA fixes for nginx. If the package also lacks shells, startup **fail-closes** with diagnostics (do not weaken this). Optional SPA-only hot path without image rebuild: [`scripts/rebuild_frontend.sh`](scripts/rebuild_frontend.sh).
- **Static sidecars:** after heal, startup runs [`compress_static_sidecars`](hpcperfstats/site/lib/compress_static_sidecars.py) over **all of `STATIC_ROOT`** (Brotli-11 / Gzip-9, mtime skip). Image `collectstatic` RUNs do the same for non-volume trees. Nginx **`brotli_static` / `gzip_static`** consume those siblings; direct sidecar URLs stay 404.
- **[`ReactSPAView`](hpcperfstats/site/hpcperfstats_site/views.py)** may read **`index.html`** from `STATIC_ROOT` / `STATICFILES_DIRS` for `/machine/` — that is **HTML shell delivery**, not serving arbitrary `/static/...` URLs from Django.

## Local development

- **`manage.py runserver`** with `DEBUG=True` normally injects static file handling for `STATIC_URL`; use **`runserver --nostatic`** when you want parity with production (no Django-served `/static/`).
- **`npm run dev`** (Vite) serves `/static/frontend/` on the dev port — **development only**; production and compose-with-`proxy` use nginx.

## Overlap

- Asset bundling and CSP for **self-hosted** scripts/styles remain under **`no-cdn-in-production.mdc`** and **`react-js-cursor-rule.mdc`**. This rule governs **which process answers the `/static/` URL**, not how assets are built.
- **`nginx-django-route-allowlist-sync.mdc`** — when adding or removing **top-level** Django routes, update the Gunicorn **`location`** allowlist in the same **`nginx-static-files.conf`** include (not only **`/static/`**).
